    <string name="receiving_needs_link_title">Receive files from %1$s in the background</string>
    <string name="receiving_needs_link_body">Android asks once whether Local Drop may be linked to this Mac. Then files from the Mac arrive even when Local Drop is closed.</string>
    <string name="receiving_link_scope">Android shows its general text about syncing, such as a caller\'s name. Local Drop does none of that: the link only lets it start receiving files in the background, with no access to contacts, calls, photos, files, messages or location. Without it, files from the Mac arrive when you tap the notification. Turn it off any time in the Mac\'s menu below.</string>
